From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:28:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: s5m: wait for the S2MPG12's read update too

The S2MPG12 (gs201: Pixel 7 and 7 Pro) has the S2MPG10's RTC registers,
and the same read update: the time registers get a copy of the counters
on a rising edge of RUDR, and the copy takes time. Commit 210e28ff7eaa
("rtc: s5m: wait for the S2MPG10's read update before reading the time")
clears RUDR, waits, sets it and waits again only on the S2MPG10, so the
S2MPG12 still reads the registers before the copy lands.

On a Pixel 7, 20 suspends through `rtcwake -m freeze -s 30` woke after
16 s four times and after 67 s once, every wake on the RTC alarm
(rtc-alarm0 counted one per suspend). Six more, each with a read of
/sys/class/rtc/rtc0/since_epoch just before rtcwake, showed that read
45 s ahead of the system clock once and 15 s behind once, while
rtcwake's own read a moment later was right and all six slept 31 s.
rtcwake sets its alarm relative to its read, so a wrong first read
moves the alarm by the same amount.

Take the S2MPG10's path on the S2MPG12 too. With it, the same 20
suspends each slept 31 s.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
index 1ac5cda1b..e38d8b918 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
@@ -357,8 +357,10 @@ static int s5m_rtc_read_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
 		 * read at once, a read could return a time seconds old, and
 		 * an alarm set from it fired early or not at all. Clear it
 		 * first and wait for the copy, as Google's s2mpg10 driver does.
+		 * The S2MPG12's RTC has the same registers and the same copy.
 		 */
-		if (info->device_type == S2MPG10) {
+		if (info->device_type == S2MPG10 ||
+		    info->device_type == S2MPG12) {
 			ret = regmap_clear_bits(info->regmap, info->regs->udr_update,
 						info->regs->read_time_udr_mask);
 			if (ret)
@@ -369,7 +371,8 @@ static int s5m_rtc_read_time(struct device *dev, struct rtc_time *tm)
 				      info->regs->read_time_udr_mask);
 		if (ret)
 			goto udr_fail;
-		if (info->device_type == S2MPG10)
+		if (info->device_type == S2MPG10 ||
+		    info->device_type == S2MPG12)
 			usleep_range(1000, 1100);
 	}
 	ret = regmap_bulk_read(info->regmap, info->regs->time, data,
